  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": 2,
  "section_notes": "The final rules keep the 55 °C test and per-model results to purchasers without public publication, but raise the sales-stop threshold to 7% with open-ended regulator-authorised interim sales, which protects Northwind's 6.2% Hearth 10. S5 replaces the numeric 8-per-100,000 recall trigger with regulator review and corrective action, with recall discretionary except for imminent serious risk, which protects Halcyon's 9.9 Ember 8. S1 reporting is 24 hours for serious incidents but excludes minor overheating and smoke events, which weakens coverage of the unreported incidents both companies disclosed."
